SUMMARY
========================================================================
TEST A: bypass-read of pointer region returned ALL 0xFF.
        → bypass-read is broken at the BAR/window level,
          OR axon-pointer bypass writes never landed either
          (and the previous 'pointers verified' was via stream).
TEST C: 0/8 small-offset round-trip matched.
        → bypass writes do NOT persist anywhere bypass-read can see.
TEST D: 0/8 bypass-writes visible to stream-read.
        → bypass and stream are accessing DIFFERENT physical HBM!
          (different channel, or different address translation)

INTERPRETATION:
  TEST A=clean + TEST D=match → bypass works for small offsets;
    issue is a write-size or chunking boundary at large offsets.
  TEST A=all-FF + TEST C=fail → bypass-read is broken regardless;
    likely BAR window mapping or ADXDMA driver issue.
  TEST D=mismatch → bypass and core access different physical HBM;
    likely PCIe-to-AXI translation in xdma IP is non-zero, or
    bypass goes to a different HBM channel than the core.
